From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: report DFS events to the correct MLO link

nl80211_radar_event() resolves the MLO link from the event frequency and
stores it in dfs_event.link_id.  nl80211_process_radar_event(), however,
always reports the event through bss->ctx, which belongs to the first link
that created the shared nl80211 BSS.

When an AP MLD spans separate 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz hostapd interfaces, a radar
event for the 5 GHz link can therefore be delivered to the 2.4 GHz hostapd
context.  The DFS handler rejects the out-of-range frequency, while the
kernel has already stopped the affected link.  CAC and NOP-finished events
are misrouted in the same way, so the 5 GHz link is not brought back.

Use the per-link context selected by dfs_event.link_id when it is present.
Keep bss->ctx as the fallback for non-MLO operation and events for which no
link could be resolved.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c | 20 +++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
@@ -2718,6 +2718,16 @@ static void nl80211_process_radar_event(
 					union wpa_event_data *data,
 					enum nl80211_radar_event event_type)
 {
+	struct i802_link *mld_link;
+	void *ctx = bss->ctx;
+
+	if (data->dfs_event.link_id != NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA &&
+	    nl80211_link_valid(bss->valid_links, data->dfs_event.link_id)) {
+		mld_link = nl80211_get_link(bss, data->dfs_event.link_id);
+		if (mld_link && mld_link->ctx)
+			ctx = mld_link->ctx;
+	}
+
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 		   "nl80211: DFS event on freq %d MHz, ht: %d, offset: %d, width: %d, cf1: %dMHz, cf2: %dMHz, link_id=%d",
 		   data->dfs_event.freq, data->dfs_event.ht_enabled,
@@ -2728,19 +2738,19 @@ static void nl80211_process_radar_event(
 
 	switch (event_type) {
 	case NL80211_RADAR_DETECTED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_RADAR_DETECTED, data);
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_RADAR_DETECTED, data);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_CAC_FINISHED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_FINISHED, data);
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_FINISHED, data);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_CAC_ABORTED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_ABORTED, data);
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_ABORTED, data);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_NOP_FINISHED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_NOP_FINISHED, data);
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_NOP_FINISHED, data);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_PRE_CAC_EXPIRED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_PRE_CAC_EXPIRED,
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_PRE_CAC_EXPIRED,
 				     data);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_CAC_STARTED:
-		wpa_supplicant_event(bss->ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_STARTED, data);
+		wpa_supplicant_event(ctx, EVENT_DFS_CAC_STARTED, data);
 		break;
 	default:
